    "title": "Highlands Cashiers Players present Dracula Double Feature and Other Haunting Treats - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Staff Reports ,\n17 hours ago The Highlands Cashiers Players lobby volunteers Jim Spencer, Amy Cooper, Janet Wilson, Barbara Lawrence, Pam Smith and Lance Scott are dressed and ready for the Dracula Double Feature. — Highlands Cashiers Players will present Dracula Double Feature and Other Haunting Treats October 15 - 25 at the Martin Lipscomb Theater in the Highlands Performing Arts Center. The evening will consist of two one-act plays, Almost the Bride of Dracula and Mid-Life Dracula, both by playwright Dennis Snee. In addition, there will be an ode to Edgar Allen Poe as performers present some of his best-known works. Randy Lucas is the director of the evening, and Cathy Myers is the production director and set designer. Read full article\n1",
    "summary": "17 hours ago The Highlands Cashiers Players lobby volunteers Jim Spencer, Amy Cooper, Janet Wilson, Barbara Lawrence, Pam Smith and Lance Scott are dressed and ready for the Dracula Double Feature. — Highlands Cashiers Players will present Dracula Double Feature and Other Haunting Treats October 15 - 25 at the Martin Lipscomb Theater in the Highlands Performing Arts Center. The evening will consist of two one-act plays, Almost the Bride of Dracula and Mid-Life Dracula, both by playwright Dennis Snee. In addition, there will be an ode to Edgar Allen Poe as performers present some of his best-known works.",
